Catalog test: run all eleven shipped examples, including arithmetic, JSON filtering and Shell tasks; require independent workspaces and retained results, preserve main bindings and catalog identities.
Execution test: preserve printed output and typed result, propagate source/check failures, replace workspace on reset.
Workbench test: save custom typed-message tools, verify target retention, reject unknown actions without replacing the previous definition.


Verify captured receiver and observed-value bindings survive an example workspace reset and that repeated runs and its check still pass with captured previous results.
